WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.110
JENNY BROWN: This week, we're
talking about everything I/O,

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.270
Tensor processing, and more.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.250
Welcome to This Week in
Cloud, where we serve

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.800
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.070
Last week was I/O, and we're
I-Overwhelmed with cool Google

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.410
things to show off.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.160
If you're looking for
one convenient place

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.320
to find all the cloud
updates, head on

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.060
over to the Google Cloud blog.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.620
We've compiled all
the announcements

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.870
and noteworthy
news into one post

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.720
full of useful information,
like exactly what's changing

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.790
and why it matters
for developers.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.190
Plus you can check out the
Google developer's blog

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:34.820
to read more about the other
areas, like Chrome and Android.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.620
Here are some of our favorites.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.512
You may already be familiar
with Tensor processing units,

00:00:39.512 --> 00:00:40.970
the chip that we
built specifically

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.710
to speed up the development
of ML applications.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.880
Well, now we're giving
you access to TPU v2

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.960
and v3 pods in beta.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.130
TPU pods are like a
supercomputer of TPUs

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.780
strapped together
and running jobs

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.330
in hours that used
to take weeks.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.730
Read more about what they
do, and try using one

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.620
in the interactive collab.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.260
From startup to
enterprise, Firebase

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.680
is all about making mobile and
web app development easier.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.360
And we saved some
big announcements

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.390
for I/O. Major
improvements to the ML Kit

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.630
bring the power of Google's
ML expertise to your app

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:17.450
through APIs like
on-device translation.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.190
Firebase Performance
Monitoring lets

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:22.100
you see how to visualize where
your web apps may be slowing

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.860
down, while the updated
Audience Builder helps

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.950
you make smarter decisions
for your user base.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.680
Read more about the details,
and build some amazing user

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.480
experiences.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.880
Everyone wants to make great
predictions with their data,

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.213
but you can't do that
without preparing it first.

00:01:37.213 --> 00:01:38.630
If you want to
transform your data

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.920
without using complex systems,
look no further than Data Prep.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.950
We've got a new blog post that
looks at how to use Data Prep,

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.350
and gives you an idea of
a three-step data quality

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.500
workflow, from assessing your
data set to resolving issues

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.240
and validating at scale.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.850
Follow along with the example,
or open up the console

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.667
and try it out on your own data.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.750
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.210
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.830
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.330
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.540
We'll see you in the cloud.

